warning[NK1261]: `ref` is redundant here: a `let` written `ref String` says what `String` already says.
   --> tests/an_element_view_of_a_text_list_is_the_one_text_view.nika:28:9
    |
 28 |         let t: ref String = w
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: Text is a view wherever a view suffices, and the ledger records whether a published parameter is lent or kept and what a result points into (ADR-282 D2). Only an `extern "C"` declaration and a `pub extern fn` write `ref String`, as the pointer C expects.
    = help: Write `String` without `ref` where the value is text of its own, and leave the type out where it is a view.
